      "Identify the specific roles of stromal cells, immune cells, and endothelial cells within tumor progression.",
      "Explain mechanisms by which TME contributes to immune evasion, angiogenesis, and metastasis.",
      "Evaluate the impact of TME on therapeutic resistance (particularly immunotherapy)."
    ],
    "key_points": [
      "Definition of TME: It includes non-cancerous cells (fibroblasts, immune cells), extracellular matrix (ECM), and signaling molecules.",
      "Major TME Subsets: Innate immune cells (TAMs, TNLMs), Myeloid-derived suppressor cells, Cancer-Associated Fibroblasts (CAFs), and Hypoxic Dendritic Cells.",
      "The 'Shield' Effect: How TME creates physical barriers for drug delivery (ECM density) and chemical barriers for immune cells (CXCL12/CCL2 chemokine signaling).",
      "Immune Evasion Mechanisms: PD-L1 upregulation by CAFs and hypoxia-induced TGF-beta signaling.",
      "Therapeutic Implications: Targeting TME (e.g., CAFs inhibition, anti-angiogenesis, immune checkpoint inhibitors requiring metabolic support)."
    ],
    "teaching_difficulties": [
      "Understanding the plasticity and heterogeneity of TME interactions (the dynamic nature of signaling).\n",
      "Connecting complex basic science mechanisms (e.g., metabolic rewiring via lactate shuttle) to patient outcomes.\n",
      "Grasping how therapeutic interventions can inadvertently shift the TME equilibrium."
    ],
