        "Transition from compensated to terminal respiratory failure"
      ]
    },
    "step_5_summary_synthesis": {
      "objective": "Connect the pieces for a coherent understanding.",
      "conclusion": "CHF is characterized by pump failure triggering maladaptive homeostatic regulators that attempt to balance but eventually worsen the clinical state (refractory edema, tachycardia)."
